herolte: kern.hero_little_idle lowers the little cluster while the screen is off (0492, D-0128)

Screen-off current is ~340 mA against 25-35 mA for Linux on this phone (E-0288, E-0434); the little cluster stays at 1066 MHz and 0.819 V. With the sysctl at 1 and the screen off for 10 s the power thread takes it to 533 MHz (boot PLL, post divider 2, the ECT dividers of 546 MHz) and 0.675 V, and back when the screen comes on, the sysctl is 0 or the phone halts. Off by default: an experiment to be measured A/B over SSH in one boot. Same primitives and boot-state check as 0465.

